-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 4, §4.6 תוספת חינוך מיוחד
-- The special-education supplement: who is a special-education teaching
-- employee, the four rates by certification and framework, and the
-- committee that may grant it retroactively.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `4.6 תוספת חינוך מיוחד`

@desc Where a teaching employee teaches, as section 4.6.2-4.6.3 distinguish it.
DECLARE `special-education framework` IS ONE OF
    `a special-education setting`
        @desc a special-education kindergarten, school or institution, a מפת"ן, or a special-education class in a regular school
    `integration in regular education`
        @desc another framework recognised in regular education, as an integration teacher or integration kindergarten teacher
    `no special-education framework`

@desc The employee's post as section 4.6 asks about it.
DECLARE `special-education post` HAS
    `employed in a framework the supervision recognised as special education` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an integration kindergarten teacher`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `an integration teacher`                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc a teacher (not of a kindergarten) working as an integration teacher in regular education
    `framework`                                  IS A `special-education framework`
    `certified for special education`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc as section 4.2 defines it; an input until 4.2 is imported
    `combined salary`                            IS A NUMBER  @desc the employee's combined salary (השכר המשולב); an input

§§ `4.6.1 Definitions`

-- akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_2__para_1/p1 The opening words of the definitions ("לעניין סעיף זה").

-- The definition's "including those employed in post-primary schools,
-- middle schools among them" widens no condition: it says the school level
-- does not matter, so no field asks for it.
-- F-4.6-a: the definition names the integration KINDERGARTEN teacher but
-- not the integration teacher of a school, whom 4.6.2(b) and 4.6.3(b) pay.
-- The reading adopted counts the integration teacher in, as those clauses
-- would otherwise pay her nothing.
@ref akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_2__para_1/p2
GIVEN p IS A `special-education post`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a special-education teaching employee` p IF
       p's `employed in a framework the supervision recognised as special education`
    OR p's `an integration kindergarten teacher`
    OR p's `an integration teacher`

-- The definition as printed, without the reading.
GIVEN p IS A `special-education post`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a special-education teaching employee as the definition prints it` p IF
       p's `employed in a framework the supervision recognised as special education`
    OR p's `an integration kindergarten teacher`

-- "Certified for special education" is section 4.2's, so it is the post's
-- input field `certified for special education`.
@ref akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_2__para_1/p3
GIVEN p IS A `special-education post`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `certified for special education under section 4.2` p IF
    p's `certified for special education`

§§ `4.6.2–4.6.3 The rates`

@ref akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_2__para_2/p1 akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_2__para_3/p1
GIVEN p IS A `special-education post`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `special-education supplement rate` p IS
    IF NOT `a special-education teaching employee` p
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `certified for special education under section 4.2` p
         THEN `the certified rate` (p's `framework`)
         ELSE `the uncertified rate` (p's `framework`)

-- "entitled to the special-education supplement at the rates as follows":
-- each rate is a share of the combined salary (השכר המשולב).
@export The special-education supplement (תוספת חינוך מיוחד) a teaching employee is owed under section 4.6 of the takanon, as a sum of money
GIVEN p IS A `special-education post` @desc the employee's post
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `special-education supplement` p IS
    `special-education supplement rate` p TIMES p's `combined salary`

@ref akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_2__para_2__subpara_a akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_2__para_2__subpara_b
GIVEN f IS A `special-education framework`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the certified rate` f IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `a special-education setting`      THEN 14%
    WHEN `integration in regular education` THEN 9%
    WHEN `no special-education framework`   THEN 0

@ref akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_2__para_3__subpara_a akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_2__para_3__subpara_b
GIVEN f IS A `special-education framework`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the uncertified rate` f IS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `a special-education setting`      THEN 8.5%
    WHEN `integration in regular education` THEN 5.5%
    WHEN `no special-education framework`   THEN 0

§§ `4.6.4 Retroactive approval`

@desc An application to the retroactive-approval committee.
DECLARE `retroactive application` HAS
    `in official (state) education`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc the applicant works in official education; otherwise for an owner (בעלות)
    `years back claimed`             IS A NUMBER  @desc how many years before the day of application the claimed entitlement reaches

DECLARE `channel of application` IS ONE OF
    `the personnel department of the district office`
    `the owner`

DECLARE `retroactive action` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the committee` HAS `through` IS A `channel of application`
    `approve retroactively`  HAS `years approved` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_2__para_4
GIVEN a IS A `retroactive application`
GIVETH A `channel of application`
DECIDE `the channel an application goes through` a IS
    IF a's `in official (state) education`
    THEN `the personnel department of the district office`
    ELSE `the owner`

-- The committee (of the teaching-personnel division, set up on the
-- Accountant-General's instructions) MAY approve up to 7 years back from
-- the day of application, and no further.
@ref akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_2__para_4
GIVEN a IS A `retroactive application`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `retroactive action`
DECIDE `retroactive approval of the supplement` a IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `apply to the committee` c PROVIDED c EQUALS `the channel an application goes through` a
    HENCE (   (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
               MAY `approve retroactively` n PROVIDED n AT MOST 7)
          RAND
              (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
               SHANT `approve retroactively` n PROVIDED n GREATER THAN 7))

-- akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_3__para_1 Source (אסמכתא): a special Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_3__para_2 Source (אסמכתא): a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_3__para_3 Source (אסמכתא): Director-General's circulars; the rates as amended by the collective agreement of 18.12.01 (encoded; its §8 is held to these rates in its tests file).
-- akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_3__para_4 Source (אסמכתא): collective agreements, a parity-committee decision and circulars.
-- akn:chp_4__sec_4_6__hc_3__para_5 Source (אסמכתא): a Director-General's circular.

-- Examples, with a placeholder combined salary of 10000 (not from a payslip).
`a certified teacher in a special-education school` MEANS
    `special-education post` WITH
        `employed in a framework the supervision recognised as special education` IS TRUE
        `an integration kindergarten teacher`         IS FALSE
        `an integration teacher`                      IS FALSE
        `framework`                                   IS `a special-education setting`
        `certified for special education`             IS TRUE
        `combined salary`                             IS 10000

`an uncertified integration teacher in a regular school` MEANS
    `special-education post` WITH
        `employed in a framework the supervision recognised as special education` IS FALSE
        `an integration kindergarten teacher`         IS FALSE
        `an integration teacher`                      IS TRUE
        `framework`                                   IS `integration in regular education`
        `certified for special education`             IS FALSE
        `combined salary`                             IS 10000

#ASSERT `special-education supplement` `a certified teacher in a special-education school` EQUALS 1400
#ASSERT `special-education supplement` `an uncertified integration teacher in a regular school` EQUALS 550

-- F-4.6-a: as the definition prints it, the integration teacher of a school
-- is not a "special-education teaching employee", so 4.6.3(b)'s rate,
-- which names her, would not reach her.
`the definition leaves out the integration teacher whom the rates pay` MEANS
    NOT `a special-education teaching employee as the definition prints it` `an uncertified integration teacher in a regular school`
#ASSERT `the definition leaves out the integration teacher whom the rates pay`

#TRACE `retroactive approval of the supplement` (`retroactive application` WITH `in official (state) education` IS TRUE, `years back claimed` IS 9) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `apply to the committee` `the personnel department of the district office` AT 1
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education` DOES `approve retroactively` 7 AT 2

§§ `Property checks`

-- The section's rules over their whole finite space: every post (recognised
-- framework or not, integration kindergarten teacher or not, integration
-- teacher or not, each framework, certified or not — 48 posts) at a
-- placeholder combined salary of 10000 (not from a payslip).

`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE
`every special-education framework` MEANS LIST `a special-education setting`, `integration in regular education`, `no special-education framework`

GIVEN rec IS A BOOLEAN, ikg IS A BOOLEAN, it IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A `special-education framework`, cert IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `special-education post`
DECIDE `a checked post` rec ikg it f cert IS
    `special-education post` WITH
        `employed in a framework the supervision recognised as special education` IS rec
        `an integration kindergarten teacher`         IS ikg
        `an integration teacher`                      IS it
        `framework`                                   IS f
        `certified for special education`             IS cert
        `combined salary`                             IS 10000

GIVEN prop IS A FUNCTION FROM `special-education post` TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds for every post` prop IF
    all (GIVEN rec YIELD
            all (GIVEN ikg YIELD
                    all (GIVEN it YIELD
                            all (GIVEN f YIELD
                                    all (GIVEN cert YIELD
                                            prop (`a checked post` rec ikg it f cert))
                                        `both booleans`)
                                `every special-education framework`)
                        `both booleans`)
                `both booleans`)
        `both booleans`

-- 4.6.2-4.6.3 over every post: the rate is one of the four the text
-- prints, or nothing; it is never above 14% nor below 0; certification
-- never pays less, and a special-education setting never less than
-- integration; a special-education teaching employee in either framework
-- the rates name is always paid; one who is not is paid nothing.
GIVEN p IS A `special-education post`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rates, for every post` p IF
        elem (`special-education supplement rate` p) (LIST 0, 14%, 9%, 8.5%, 5.5%)
    AND `special-education supplement` p AT LEAST 0
    AND `special-education supplement` p AT MOST 14% TIMES p's `combined salary`
    AND `special-education supplement rate` (`a checked post` (p's `employed in a framework the supervision recognised as special education`) (p's `an integration kindergarten teacher`) (p's `an integration teacher`) (p's `framework`) TRUE)
        AT LEAST `special-education supplement rate` p
    AND `special-education supplement rate` (`a checked post` (p's `employed in a framework the supervision recognised as special education`) (p's `an integration kindergarten teacher`) (p's `an integration teacher`) `a special-education setting` (p's `certified for special education`))
        AT LEAST `special-education supplement rate` (`a checked post` (p's `employed in a framework the supervision recognised as special education`) (p's `an integration kindergarten teacher`) (p's `an integration teacher`) `integration in regular education` (p's `certified for special education`))
    AND ((NOT `a special-education teaching employee` p)
         OR p's `framework` EQUALS `no special-education framework`
         OR `special-education supplement rate` p GREATER THAN 0)
    AND (`a special-education teaching employee` p
         OR `special-education supplement rate` p EQUALS 0)
#ASSERT `holds for every post` `the rates, for every post`

-- F-4.6-a over every post: as the definition prints it, an integration
-- teacher of a school who is neither employed in a recognised framework nor
-- an integration kindergarten teacher is never a special-education teaching
-- employee, though 4.6.2(b) and 4.6.3(b) name her; under the reading she is
-- paid in the integration framework whether certified or not.
GIVEN p IS A `special-education post`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the definition and the rates part on the integration teacher` p IF
        (NOT (    p's `an integration teacher`
              AND (NOT p's `employed in a framework the supervision recognised as special education`)
              AND (NOT p's `an integration kindergarten teacher`)))
    OR (    (NOT `a special-education teaching employee as the definition prints it` p)
        AND ((NOT (p's `framework` EQUALS `integration in regular education`))
             OR `special-education supplement rate` p GREATER THAN 0))
#ASSERT `holds for every post` `the definition and the rates part on the integration teacher`

-- 4.6.4 at its bound: seven years back is within the committee's power,
-- eight is not.
#TRACE `retroactive approval of the supplement` (`retroactive application` WITH `in official (state) education` IS FALSE, `years back claimed` IS 8) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `apply to the committee` `the owner` AT 1
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education` DOES `approve retroactively` 8 AT 2
